<main class="container academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/blog'>Learning library</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">lesson <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1>Web Performance and User Experience Guide</h1><p>Performance is part of usability: pages should show meaningful content quickly, remain stable as they load, and respond reliably to keyboard, touch and pointer input.</p></section><div class="academy-reading-layout"><aside class="academy-toc"><p class="academy-kicker">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#section-1"><span>01</span>Prioritize what appears first</a><a href="#section-2"><span>02</span>Size images deliberately</a><a href="#section-3"><span>03</span>Reduce font-loading delays</a><a href="#section-4"><span>04</span>Test responsive behavior</a><a href="#section-5"><span>05</span>Measure rather than assume</a></nav><div class="academy-author"><img src="/assets/images/mbk-personal-favicon-96.png" width="38" height="38" alt=""><div>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Founder, MBK Global</small></div></div><p class="academy-read-note">2 min read · Practical learning notes<br>Learn. Apply. Make it your own.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>More learning resources ↗</a></aside><div class="academy-reading-body"><article class="content-page"><header><p class="eyebrow">MBK Global · Practical guide</p></header><section><h2 id="section-1">Prioritize what appears first</h2><p>Identify the primary above-the-fold content and avoid lazy-loading the main visual when it is needed for the initial experience. Use fetch priority only for a genuinely important image and do not preload every asset.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-2">Size images deliberately</h2><p>Set width and height attributes when dimensions are known so the browser can reserve space. Use responsive image sizes where practical, preserve aspect ratio, and lazy-load suitable below-the-fold images. Do not rehost third-party images without permission.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-3">Reduce font-loading delays</h2><p>Avoid CSS @import chains for web fonts. Use explicit stylesheet links and preconnect only to origins actually needed. Provide a sensible fallback stack and use font-display: swap when self-hosting or configuring fonts.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-4">Test responsive behavior</h2><p>Check representative narrow mobile widths, tablet and desktop layouts. Look for horizontal overflow, clipped navigation, unreadable text, tap targets that are too small and forms that are hard to complete.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-5">Measure rather than assume</h2><p>Core Web Vitals goals are LCP at or below 2.5 seconds, INP at or below 200 milliseconds and CLS at or below 0.1. These are targets, not results; distinguish local lab tests from real-user field data and retest after deployment.</p></section>
<p><strong>About this guide:</strong> This is general educational guidance. Adapt recommendations to your site's actual stack, risk and audience, and verify changes before publishing.</p>
<p>Explore related work: <a href='/web-development'>web development</a>, <a href='/projects'>projects</a>, and <a href='/contact'>contact</a>.</p></article></div></div><div data-portrait-track data-caption="The person behind the work"></div></main>
